= Client-server model — Simple =

The client-server model is a distributed-computing pattern in which a client initiates requests for services or resources and a server provides responses or services.

Client and server are interaction roles, not permanent identities of physical machines. A system can act as a client in one relationship and a server in another.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* client/server role ≠ permanent machine identity
* client-server ≠ centralized system necessarily

